Vector palettization (`cluster_dim > 1`) now selects its k-means backend from the device rather than defaulting to the torch implementation: `flash_kmeans` on CUDA when installed, otherwise `cuml`, otherwise the previous `kmeans++`. A sensitivity-weighted run skips `flash_kmeans`, which has no `sample_weight` equivalent. The default number of restarts is now 12, set independently of the backend — `COREAI_KMEANS_BACKEND` and `COREAI_KMEANS_N_INIT` override the two separately, and changing one never moves the other. Measured on Qwen3-4B (8-bit, `cluster_dim=2`, `group_size=32`, 252 tensors, single worker): 4737s at 17.1599 wikitext perplexity for `flash_kmeans` at 12 restarts, against 39228s at 17.5235 for the previous default — 8.3x faster and 0.36 perplexity better. `cuml` reaches 17.2234 at 4 restarts and 17.1153 at 5, so lower `COREAI_KMEANS_N_INIT` when using it if clustering time matters more than quality. `num_workers` is additionally reduced to 1 for an all-vector model on a GPU-resident backend, since one device serialises that work and extra processes only add CUDA context switching (measured 2.05x slower at 12 workers).
